n at 15 Dec 2026.** New MRR = 80,000 − 7,200 = **$72,800** (−9.0%); new ARR = 800×... = 72,800 × 12 = **$873,600** (−$86,400); 27 customers. Constant-burn: new burn = 295,061 + 7,200 = **$302,261/mo**; 6,019,000 ÷ 302,261 = **19.91 months** (−0.49 mo, ≈15 days). Timing-adjusted (loss starts 15 Dec): cash at 15 Dec = 6,019,000 − 2.5×295,061 = $5,281,348; ÷302,261 = 17.47 mo → cash-zero **~30 May 2028** vs ~11 Jun 2028 baseline. GRR (87.4%) and NRR (97.9%) both fall further — I can't restate them precisely (aggregate mrr-by-month.csv gives GRR ~74.5% on a beginning-MRR basis, so the summary uses a cohort method the files don't document).\\n\\n**3. Credit + churn.** $1,440 + loss ⇒ zero date ~1.5 days earlier than churn alone. Credit is noise (0.5% of the ARR at risk).\\n\\n**4. Second-order.** FP-2001: $7,200 ACH, 4 failures, next retry 14 Oct, vendor-portal issue; in this dataset 2 of 3 repeat-failure ACH accounts (FP-2008, FP-2011) later churned — leading indicator. 5% uplift cap = **$4,320/yr**; the $2,160 ask is **half a year's maximum price increase**. Clause 9.3 (uptime <99.5% in 3 of 6 months; Aug was 99.1%) gives Northwind a for-cause exit independent of the 16 Oct window. Precedent risk: Aug 14 outage also hit Tessera/Meridian/Brightwave (amounts not in files). Q3 churn $8,100 + $7,200 = **$15,300 MRR (19.1% of base)** in two quarters; 2026 YTD churn $16,700.\\n\\n**5. Break-even.** $1,440 ÷ $7,200 = **0.2 months ≈ 6.1 days** of retained revenue; equivalently $1,440 ÷ $86,400 = **1.7pp** of 12-month retention probability.\\n\\n**Recommendation:** grant the $2,160, but only against the 14 Oct invoice clearing and a written renewal confirmation before 16 Oct; otherwise hold at $720. Capture the 5% uplift ($4,320) to net +$2,160 in year 1. Sources: finance/summary.md, finance/stripe-export/{failed-payments,customers,mrr-by-month}.csv, legal/contracts-register.csv, customer-success/churn-log.md. No cfo.ai changes made.\"},{\"span_id\":\"96c7d94991a3191d\",\"name\